      "observed": "U14 is a powered SN74LVC1G07 buffer: pin 1 (/OE) is on NET0062, pin 2 (A) is on Net-(U14-A), pin 3 is GND, and pin 5 is +3V3, but pin 4 (Y) does not appear on any net in the netlist.",
      "expected": "The output of an enabled/powered buffer used in the e-stop or indicator path should be connected to its intended signal net; leaving Y floating makes the intended sink/drive path incomplete.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U14\") (value \"SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1\") ... (libsource (lib \"acorn-motherboard\") (part \"SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(libpart (lib \"acorn-motherboard\") (part \"SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1\") ... (pin (num \"4\") (name \"Y\") (type \"output\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"207\") (name \"Net-(U14-A)\") ... (node (ref \"U14\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"input\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "an e-stop loop with multiple sink points ... gated through single non-inverting buffers ... feeding an ESTOP_OUT signal"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The signal path driven by U14 is broken. If U14 is one of the e-stop sink buffers, its intended pull-down/sink action cannot occur, potentially changing e-stop behavior or leaving an associated indicator/sink undefined.",
      "confidence": 0.82
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": [
        "Module2",
        "SW7",
        "SW1",
        "R86"
      ],
      "pins": [
        "Module2.99",
        "SW7.2",
        "SW1.2"
      ],
      "nets": [
        "NET0119",
        "NET0037"
      ],
      "observed": "Module2 pin 99 (Global_EN) is connected only to SW7 pin 2 on NET0119. The specified switch SW1 pin 2 is on NET0037 with pull-up R86 to +3V3, but NET0037 is not connected to Global_EN.",
      "expected": "The specification states the CM4 power-enable path GLOBAL_EN is tied directly to SW1 pin 2, giving the enable signal to the switch/pull-up node rather than to a different switch.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "Module1 pin 99 (Global_EN) — GLOBAL_EN net, tied directly to SW1 pin 2"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"101\") (name \"NET0119\") ... (node (ref \"Module2\") (pin \"99\") (pinfunction \"Global_EN\") (pintype \"input\")) ... (node (ref \"SW7\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"71\") (name \"NET0037\") ... (node (ref \"R86\") (pin \"2\") ... ) ... (node (ref \"SW1\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"B\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The CM4 power-enable input is connected to the wrong switch node and may float or be controlled by an unintended path, which can prevent reliable power-on or make the board behave differently from the intended direct power-enable switch design.",
      "confidence": 0.74
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": [
        "U45",
        "U48"
      ],
      "pins": [
        "U45.4",
        "U45.5",
        "U48.4",
        "U48.5"
      ],
      "nets": [
        "GND"
      ],
      "observed": "The isolated CAN transceivers U45 and U48 have both GND1 and GND2 pins tied to the common GND net.",
      "expected": "For isolated CAN buses, the transceiver primary ground (GND1) and secondary ground (GND2) should remain separate isolated grounds; tying them together defeats galvanic isolation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (CAN0, CAN1), each driven by its own MCP2515 SPI CAN controller ... through an isolated CAN transceiver"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"53\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"U45\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND1\") (pintype \"power_in\")) ... (node (ref \"U45\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\") (pintype \"power_in\")) ... (node (ref \"U48\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND1\") (pintype \"power_in\")) ... (node (ref \"U48\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\") (pintype \"power_in\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The CAN interfaces are not galvanically isolated despite using isolated transceiver parts, so ground loops or common-mode currents can propagate between the rover power/motor domain and the CAN bus domain.",
      "confidence": 0.7
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist shows at least one clear connectivity anomaly: U14's buffer output is unconnected. It also deviates from the stated CM4 power-enable design and ties the isolated CAN transceiver grounds together, defeating the intended CAN isolation."
}

